<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The thinking mark: a brain, from Lucide's `brain`.

    Lucide is ISC-licensed and draws on the same 24dp grid as the Material set this
    app uses everywhere else, so the mark sits beside them without a second visual
    language. The path data is copied verbatim; only the stroke colour differs, and
    `Icon`'s own tint replaces that anyway.

    Why a mark of its own rather than a Material glyph: this row used
    `Icons.Filled.Psychology`, which is a *head with a gear in it* — a picture of a
    person, not of the act of thinking, and at 15dp the head reads as a blob. The
    reference the reader pointed at uses a brain, Material has no brain, and the
    same reasoning that produced `ic_model.xml` applies here: one custom vector
    costs less than a glyph that says the wrong thing.

    Lucide's own `brain` also carries six short hair-line ticks (at the crown, the
    temples and the jaw). They are omitted: at 15dp they are sub-pixel, and what is
    left — two halves and the seam between them — is the shape that reads.

    Stroked rather than filled, the same way `ic_model.xml` is: Material's own
    outlined weight is 2/24 too, and a filled brain at 15dp is one solid blob.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
        android:strokeWidth="2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M12 5a3 3 0 1 0-5.997.125 4 4 0 0 0-2.526 5.77 4 4 0 0 0 .556 6.588A4 4 0 1 0 12 18Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
        android:strokeWidth="2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M12 5a3 3 0 1 1 5.997.125 4 4 0 0 1 2.526 5.77 4 4 0 0 1-.556 6.588A4 4 0 1 1 12 18Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
        android:strokeWidth="2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M15 13a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-3-4 4.5 4.5 0 0 1-3 4" />
</vector>
